# Rules

Normative one-sentence rules with their scope, enforcing control, and sources. A Rule is the transferable half of what would otherwise live only in an agent's memory.

Most rules are one row and nothing more. A linked rule name has a detail document alongside it carrying the reason, worked examples, and agent instructions.

## Rules

| Rule | Status | Scope | Enforcement | Control | Sources | Statement |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| [alpha-rule](alpha-rule/README.md) | Active | fleet | Enforced | wb pre-commit hook | lesson:a | Always do the alpha thing before the beta thing. |
| beta-rule | Draft | path:**/*.go | Stated | — | — | Never do the beta thing without the alpha thing. |

